-- title:
--   Crossing point in the j-finite chart of the integral model
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$, let $A$ act on $K$ compatibly with $A \to L \to K$, let $j \in K$ be an element whose image in $L((q))$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ`), with $j \neq 0$, and let $\varpi$ be a generator of the maximal ideal of $A$. Then there is a point $y$ of the finite chart $\mathrm{XFin}\,A\,K\,j = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebra `chartAlgFin A K j` of $K$ such that, writing $x$ for the image of $y$ under the canonical morphism `ιFin` into the two-chart integral model $X = \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ (the pushout of the two chart inclusions), the ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ generated by the germ at $x$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ via the structure morphism $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ has a set of minimal primes that is not a subsingleton, i.e. has at least two elements.
--
--   This is the statement that the special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ has a crossing lying in the $j$-finite chart: a point through which two branches of the fibre pass, classically a supersingular point where the two Igusa components meet. It is used in the analysis of the special fibre of this model, in the statement that the relevant pullback is reduced and has positive cardinality.
